{"uid":"7da4dfb80fb15765","name":"test_a_live_ruling_the_table_refuses_is_reported_once_not_once_per_boundary","fullName":"tests.test_amendment_status_load_time#test_a_live_ruling_the_table_refuses_is_reported_once_not_once_per_boundary","historyId":"5ff3ddbd4cb2c2b93a4db9f0908e9c58","time":{"start":1791935163658,"stop":1791935163665,"duration":7},"description":"A ruling ordering `in-progress -> pending` is refused, not forced:\n    nothing in `transitions.TASK_STATUS_TABLE` names `pending` as a\n    successor of anything, so the declared table already enforces the house\n    rule and the boundary re-read inherits it for free.\n\n    The refusal must also be BOUNDED. Reported once per episode it needed no\n    dedupe at all; reported once per boundary it would be one `log` line per\n    iteration for the rest of the run, which is why\n    `_status_ruling_refusals_reported` exists. Two drives of the boundary,\n    exactly one REFUSED line -- this node is what fails if that dedupe is\n    dropped, and its `previous` component is what keeps a genuinely changed\n    situation reportable.","descriptionHtml":"<p>A ruling ordering <code>in-progress -&gt; pending</code> is refused, not forced:<br />\nnothing in <code>transitions.TASK_STATUS_TABLE</code> names <code>pending</code> as a<br />\nsuccessor of anything, so the declared table already enforces the house<br />\nrule and the boundary re-read inherits it for free.</p>\n<pre><code>The refusal must also be BOUNDED. Reported once per episode it needed no\ndedupe at all; reported once per boundary it would be one `log` line per\niteration for the rest of the run, which is why\n`_status_ruling_refusals_reported` exists. Two drives of the boundary,\nexactly one REFUSED line -- this node is what fails if that dedupe is\ndropped, and its `previous` component is what keeps a genuinely changed\nsituation reportable.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesC